14636      data Neuralgia;
14637      input Treatment $ Sex $ Age Duration Pain $ @@;
14638      datalines;

NOTE: SAS went to a new line when INPUT statement reached past the end of a line.
NOTE: The data set WORK.NEURALGIA has 60 observations and 5 variables.

14660      ;
14661      run;
14662      proc logistic data=Neuralgia;
14663      class Treatment Sex / param=glm;
14664      model Pain= Treatment|Sex Age;
14665      oddsratio Treatment;
14666      lsmeans Treatment / e diff oddsratio cl adjust=bon;
14667      run;

NOTE: PROC LOGISTIC is modeling the probability that Pain='No'. One way to change this to model the probability that Pain='Yes' is to specify the response 
      variable option EVENT='Yes'.
NOTE: Convergence criterion (GCONV=1E-8) satisfied.
NOTE: There were 60 observations read from the data set WORK.NEURALGIA.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE LOGISTIC printed page 1220.

14668      proc logistic data=Neuralgia;
14669      class Treatment Sex / param=glm;
14670      model Pain= Treatment|Sex Age;
14671      lsmestimate treatment 1 0 -1, 0 1 -1 / joint;
14672      run;

NOTE: PROC LOGISTIC is modeling the probability that Pain='No'. One way to change this to model the probability that Pain='Yes' is to specify the response 
